-Response-from-CQC.pdf","promises":[],"unmatched":true}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/nicola-forster-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Nicola Forster: Prevention of future deaths report","date":"2024-06-20","coroner":"Emma Whitting","area":"Bedfordshire and Luton","ref":"2024-0334","categories":["Suicide (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/2024-0334-Response-from-Metropolitan-Police.pdf","filename":"2024-0334-Response-from-Metropolitan-Police.pdf","promises":[],"unmatched":true}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/neil-woodley-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Neil Woodley: Prevention of Future Deaths Report","date":"2024-07-23","coroner":"Jonathan Landau","area":"South London","ref":"2024-0414","categories":["Suicide (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2024-0414-Response-from-Metropolitan-Police.pdf","filename":"2024-0414-Response-from-Metropolitan-Police.pdf","promises":[]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/zara-aleena-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Zara Aleena: Prevention of Future Deaths Report","date":"2024-07-26","coroner":"Nadia Persaud","area":"East London","ref":"2024-0409","categories":["Other related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2024-0409-Response-from-London-Borough-of-Redbridge.pdf","filename":"2024-0409-Response-from-London-Borough-of-Redbridge.pdf","promises":[{"id":655,"quote":"The training for CCTV operators encompasses modules that cover behavioural body language training and are specifically designed to detect behaviours that would fall under the remit of 'suspicious'. The training is based on established principles and techniques outlined in Tavcom training programs - suspicious behaviours can include gestures, mannerisms, alone or in a group, time, location, how someone is acting (i.e. drunk/disorientated), approaching people, being aggressive etc. The training given","summary":"Introduce annual mandatory refresher training for CCTV operators on suspicious behaviour","timescale":"annual"}]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2024-0409-Response-from-Metropolitan-Police.pdf","filename":"2024-0409-Response-from-Metropolitan-Police.pdf","promises":[{"id":1563,"quote":"The MPS accepts that the reviews of this case lacked sufficient rigour and detail and that the review process was not sufficiently comprehensive to identify all the potential learning arising from the police response.","summary":"Accepts review process lacked rigour and will improve independence.","timescale":"later in 2024"}]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2024-0409-Response-from-HMPPS-and-MoJ.pdf","filename":"2024-0409-Response-from-HMPPS-and-MoJ.pdf","promises":[{"id":1677,"quote":"We accept that the Probation Delivery Unit (PDU) responsible for Jordan McSweeney was understaffed at the time. Whilst at a national level, the staffing position of the Probation Service is improving, I acknowledge that raising staffing in this PDU to its full complement remains a significant challenge. Therefore, until such time as the situation improves, in this PDU and others with acute pressure remaining, staff will follow a Prioritisation Framework which we first implemented in January 2022","summary":"Implement Prioritisation Framework to manage staffing pressures","timescale":"January 2022"}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/peter-jones-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Peter Jones: Prevention of Future Deaths Report","date":"2025-02-04","coroner":"Mary Hassell","area":"Inner North London","ref":"2025-0066","categories":["Suicide (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Peter-Jones-Narrati